# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
#
# Device identity is a TPM 2.0 attestation key rather than a private
# key held in NVRAM.  src/interface/efi/efi_tpm2.c creates a restricted
# signing key inside the TPM (TPM2_CreatePrimary, ECC P-256 with an
# RSA-2048 fallback), makes it persistent (TPM2_EvictControl, handle
# 0x81000001) and reuses it on every later boot: no code path here
# overwrites or rebuilds an existing key.  Raw TPM 2.0 commands are
# submitted through the EFI_TCG2_PROTOCOL SubmitCommand() service,
# which is the standard EFI route to the TPM; that protocol exposes no
# Quote operation, so TPM2_Quote is issued directly and the PCR
# 0/2/4/7 digest and the signature are produced by a single TPM call.
#
# src/hci/commands/ak_cmd.c adds the akgen, akpub and quote commands.
# akpub also reads the EFI SecureBoot global variable and publishes it
# as the "sb" setting (1 = enabled, 0 = disabled) for the device report.
#
# The exported encodings match the control plane verifier:
# SubjectPublicKeyInfo DER for ak-public, TPM2B_NAME (0x000b followed
# by the SHA-256 of the public area) for ak-name, raw TPMS_ATTEST
# without the TPM2B length prefix for quote, and ECDSA DER or
# RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 over the raw TPMS_ATTEST bytes for quote-sig.  The
# nonce is copied into extraData verbatim as ASCII bytes.  All five
# settings live in the in-memory settings root for the current boot
# only and never reach the EFI variable NVS backend.
#
# Without a TPM (no TCG2 protocol) or without a key they fail with
# -ENODEV / -ENOENT and nothing else, so a boot script can follow its
# no-TPM path; there is no software fallback.
#
# All new files carry FILE_LICENCE ( GPL2_OR_LATER_OR_UBDL ); the
# modifications to the iPXE configuration and headers inherit the
# upstream licence (GPL-2.0-or-later / UBDL).

